ALLOWAY: All of us participate in the social construct to some degree and win it.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: But if I don`t, that`s what law enforcement is for.\par \par \uc2 CALLOWAY: Yeah, but I mean, you know, we`re also trying to win elections. We`re also trying to appeal to a middle of the road, white voter, and what does that look like, if I drag a bunch of white guys in and do perp walks with them, take them up out of their country club. It`s a tough spot for Democrats to be in. It`s an extraordinarily tough spot, and I think you hit the nail on the head and pointing out the sensitivities there.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Michael Steele, rebuttal?\par \par \uc2 STEELE: I mean, it`s not so much a rebuttal. I mean, look, we`re kind of in the same space my only thing is, you have the power, you have the authority that is given to you under the Constitution and the rules of the Commission, they explicitly set out that they had subpoena power. Well, if you have the power, that means you should use the power. And it`s not a question of them not using it. The question is, will you use it? And when will you use it to enforce it?\par \par \uc2 Look, you know, Bannon and others can hold out and not appear. But when the marshal show up at their doorstep, that`s a whole different conversation, when they then have to go get lawyers to deal with that. That`s a whole different reality.\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you about the GOP expectation is, you`re not going to do it, you don`t have what it takes to do it. That`s what they`re betting.\par \par \uc2 CALLOWAY: Listen.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: No, I mean very serious. I hear you. I hear you.\par \par \uc2 CALLOWAY: I want you to keep this same energy, when two months from now Joe Biden decides he has the power and the constitutional authority to add to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: He does, if he wants to do it and use it. Well, they can`t -- you can`t even decide to do the filibuster. So, I`m not worried about what you`re going to do in the Supreme Court, OK, so listen --\par \par \uc2 CALLOWAY: Gut check time for Joe Biden and House Democrats as well. You`re absolutely right, they have the authority, but you act as though we know understand his political realities. And he has to protect his house majorities as well as become reelected himself for doing these things.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: Understood, but I would think that January 6 -- what happened on January 6, Trump`s and to use that term deliberately, Trump`s the political vagrancies or realities or whatever they are for either party, our country --\par \par \uc2 CALLOWAY: I think you`re exactly right, but you don`t have single elected Republican who, other than Adam Kinzinger, who has stood up in the middle of the public square and said that let`s talk about preserving democracy over preserving Trumpsm.\par \par \uc2 STEELE: True, but you got subpoena power, so use it.\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: Let me -- I have commercial power, let me just butt in here. To our viewers, I`ve been watching this too. There`s nothing like when Morehouse and Johns Hopkins get together, it gets sporty, but we have to fit in a break. Both of these gentlemen are going to stay with us.\par \par \uc2 Coming up, divisions among the Democrats themselves on full display these days. And look at who`s trying to capitalize on it.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 [23:33:00]\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. CHUCK SCHUMER, (D) NEW YORK MAJORITY LEADER: Republicans played a dangerous and risky partisan game. And I am glad that their brinksmanship did not work. Senate Republicans insisted they wanted a solution to the debt ceiling but said Democrats must raise it alone by going through a drawn out, convoluted and risky reconciliation process. That was simply unacceptable to my caucus. And yesterday, Senate Republicans finally realized that their obstruction was not going to work.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS: 