d Trump\uc2  said the election was stolen from him. This Saturday was the day Trump supporters were going to demand the release of all the people arrested for their alleged roles in that attack back on January 6th.\par \par \uc2 [21:05:06]\par \par \uc2 You know, including the people who smashed in the windows of the \uc2 Capitol\uc2  and beat cops with metal pipes and crutches and hockey sticks and sprayed police officers with bear spray and hit them with stun guns. The point of this rally on Saturday was to agitate for all of those people to be freed because obviously they`re just being persecuted for being Trump supporters. They didn`t do anything wrong.\par \par \uc2 That was the cause around which Trump supporters organized this rally on Saturday. But, like, no matter the size of the dog, it ended up being just like dude and his dog. Saturday ended up being a story of over preparedness by \uc2 Capitol police\uc2  thank God, which is better than the opposite. They did arrest a couple people on outstanding warrants, somebody else on a weapons charge. But the fencing going back up around the us you Capitol and the National Guard standing by turns out was not what was needed.\par \par \uc2 Man with dog and impromptu exercise class not with standing, nobody really showed up. That said, the cause is alive. The Republican legislators are busy pursuing their own efforts to overturn or try to discredit the presidential election results. The Republican investigation of the presidential election results from Wisconsin, they have now set up their own \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel to try to make their investigation of the election results seem more official.\par \par \uc2 As we`ve been reporting here over the last couple weeks so far this investigation has been conducting its business using a random Gmail address and fake letterhead they made up. Now they`ve got a \uc2 YouTube\uc2  channel. And so Wisconsin Republicans are trying to make it all seem much more official.\par \par