 \uc2 John Durham\uc2  and the Durham investigation apparently furious that Durham hadn`t put out a report before the 2020 election, something Attorney General Bill Barr reportedly pressured \uc2 John Durham\uc2  to do.\par \par \uc2 Since out of office, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has continued to rail about \uc2 John Durham\uc2 . Where is Durham`s damning report? Where are the indictments? Why are my enemies not all in handcuffs?\par \par \uc2 For years now, the Durham investigation has been the holy grail for Trump and his supporters the thing that will expose the Russia investigation as some crime against Trump that itself must be avenged.\par \par \uc2 And one of the angles Durham has been working on is the theory which was originally advanced by this Kremlin-connected Russian bank, \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2 , this theory that \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  and the \uc2 Trump Organization\uc2  were framed by computer scientists who supposedly found communications between the servers, computer scientists who discussed those communications and passed it on to the press and passed it on to the \uc2 FBI\uc2  for investigation.\par \par \uc2 Dexter Filkins at "The New Yorker" reporting almost a year ago that Durham was actually hauling in the computer scientist that has raised these concerns about \uc2 Alfa Bank\uc2  and putting them before a grand jury.\par \par \uc2 Well, here is what has broken tonight in "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 ." quote, \uc2 John Durham\uc2 , special counsel appointed by the Trump administration to scrutinize the Russia investigation has told the Justice Department he will ask a grand jury to indict a prominent cyber lawyer on a charge of making a false statement to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 . Any indictment of the lawyer, Michael Sussman, a former federal prosecutor now, excuse me, now a partner the \uc2 Perkins Coie\uc2  law firm who represented the DNC on issues related to Russia`s 2016 hacking of the servers, any indictment of Sussman is likely to attract significant