nything else the justice department should or could be doing now, in the short term that would make a difference?\par \par \uc2 CYNTHIA ALKSNE, FORMER FEDERAL PROSECUTOR: You know, I really don`t think there is, and that`s the problem.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: OK.\par \par \uc2 ALKSNE: You know, you can protect those people who are seeking an abortion, who are, you know, fit within the Texas statute prior to six weeks. You know, there`s a lot of talk about trying to use 241 and 242, which are the Civil Rights statutes, but I don`t think that`s going to happen.\par \par \uc2 I mean, because given that the Supreme Court has said, this statue can go forward, Garland`s hands are really tied. I mean, I would like some action, but I have to say, I don`t think you can really criticize the Attorney General at this point. He does -- doesn`t have a lot of options.\par \par \uc2 We really need the Congress to act. I mean, there`s all this discussion about well, that they shouldn`t bother because they can`t get the votes, and they can`t grow with the filibuster, and they can`t, they can`t, they can`t, they can`t.\par \par \uc2 And you know, I`m over that. Like, you know, what, put something on the floor and get a vote and put people on notice. And if you can`t get it now, then we`ll run against them and we`ll have a record.\par \par \uc2 But the Republicans have been able to sort of hiding behind this, we haven`t put anything on the floor, they`ve been able to hide and get away with it for a long time, and that`s part of the problem. I think we need to put people on the record now and regularly in abortion -- you know, a Choice Act.\par \par \uc2 And then, a Choice Act with or without exceptions for rape and incest and come up with creative acts over and over and over so that the Republicans have to make a record and we can beat them. Because the American people support having a woman be able to control her own body and let`s take advantage of that.\par \par \uc2 JACKSON: You`re 